2$ galaxies are \[C II\]  deficient and investigate what are the main physical parameters the \[C II\]  emission line is sensitive to."}]},"targets":[{"name":"10 main-sequence galaxies in GOODS-S (IDs 9347, 6515, 10076, 9834, 9681, 10049, 2861, 2910, 7118, 8490)","details":[{"loc":"2.1 Sample selection and ancillary data","quote":"we selected targets in the GOODS-S field ((cite: Giavalisco2004), (cite: Nonino2009))"},{"loc":"2.1 Sample selection and ancillary data","quote":"having spectroscopic redshift in the range $1.73 < z < 1.94$"}],"coordinates":"Table 1 lists RA/Dec per galaxy (e.g. ID9347: 53.154900, -27.809397 deg)","redshift_or_distance":"1.73 < z < 1.94 (spectroscopic)","distance_source":"Spectroscopic redshifts from GMASS, K20, Popesso2009, Keck/LRIS, Pope2008, refined via Gobat2017 template fitting"}],"alma_project_codes":[{"code":"2012.1.00775.S","evidence":[{"loc":"2.2 Details of ALMA observations","quote":"during Cycle 1 (PI: E. Daddi, Project ID: 2012.1.00775.S)"}]}],"data_settings":[{"field":"bands","value":"Band 9 ([C II], 450 um continuum) and Band 7 (850 um continuum)","evidence":[{"loc":"2.2 Details of ALMA observations","quote":"we also requested additional observations in Band 7 to detect the 850 $\mu$m continuum"}]},{"field":"frequencies_and_spectral_setup","value":"nu_obs = 645-696 GHz; four 1.875 GHz sidebands; 0.976 MHz channels","evidence":[{"loc":"2.2 Details of ALMA observations","quote":"redshifted in the frequency range $\nu_{\mathrm{obs}} = 645$ – $696$ GHz"},{"loc":"2.2 Details of ALMA observations","quote":"We set a spectral resolution of 0.976 MHz"}]},{"field":"configurations","value":"C32-3 (C32-1 requested)","evidence":[{"loc":"2.2 Details of ALMA observations","quote":"the observations were taken in the C32-3 configuration"}]},{"field":"angular_resolution","value":"Band 9: 0.3" x 0.2"},{"field":"max_recoverable_scale","value":"~3.5" (Band 9); ~6" (Band 7)","evidence":[{"loc":"2.2 Details of ALMA observations","quote":"a maximum recoverable scale of $\sim$ 3.5”"},{"loc":"2.2 Details of ALMA observations","quote":"the maximum recoverable scale is $\sim$ 6”"}]},{"field":"sensitivity","value":"Band 7 continuum 140 uJy/beam; Band 9 target 1.5-2 mJy/beam over 350 km/s; per-source rms 11.6-51 mJy/beam (Table log)","evidence":[{"loc":"2.2 Details of ALMA observations","quote":"For each galaxy we reached a sensitivity of 140 $\mu$Jy/beam on the continuum"}]},{"field":"time_on_source","value":"Band 9: 9.6-17.1 min per galaxy; Band 7 ~2 min","evidence":[{"loc":"2.2 Details of ALMA observations","quote":"with an integration time of $\sim 2$ minutes on source"}]},{"field":"observing_dates","value":"03-04 Nov 2013","evidence":[{"loc":"Table 1 (log)","quote":"| 9347 | 03 Nov 2013 |"}]},{"field":"pi_or_archival_as_stated","value":"Cycle 1, PI E. Daddi","evidence":[{"loc":"2.2 Details of ALMA observations","quote":"during Cycle 1 (PI: E. Daddi, Project ID: 2012.1.00775.S)"}]}],"lines_targeted":[{"species":"[C II]","transition":"2P3/2-2P1/2 (158 um)","rest_frequency":"1900.54 GHz","evidence":[{"loc":"2.2 Details of ALMA observations","quote":"$\nu_{\mathrm{rest-frame}} = 1900.54$ GHz"}]}],"other_facilities":[{"name":"HST (CANDELS)","provided":{"value":"Optical/near-IR imaging for sizes, stellar mass and SFR maps","evidence":[{"loc":"2.1 Sample selection and ancillary data","quote":"Deep Hubble Space Telescope (*HST*) observations at optical"}]}},{"name":"Spitzer and Herschel","provided":{"value":"24-500 um photometry for IR SED fitting","evidence":[{"loc":"2.1 Sample selection and ancillary data","quote":"*Spitzer* and *Herschel* mid-IR and far-IR photometry in the wavelength range 24 $\mu$m – 500 $\mu$m is also available"}]}},{"name":"VLA","provided":{"value":"6 GHz radio imaging, positions consistent with ALMA","evidence":[{"loc":"2.1 Sample selection and ancillary data","quote":"radio observations at $\sim$ 5 cm (6 GHz) were taken with the Karl G. Jansky Very Large Array (VLA)"}]}},{"name":"VLT and Keck spectroscopy","provided":{"value":"Optical spectroscopic redshifts","evidence":[{"loc":"2.1 Sample selection and ancillary data","quote":"one was estimated from our rest-frame UV Keck/LRIS spectroscopy"}]}}],"external_data_from_literature":[{"what":{"value":"Literature [C II], IR, CO luminosities, gas masses, sSFR, metallicities for local and high-z samples (Appendix C)","evidence":[{"loc":"2.5 Other samples from the literature","quote":"we complemented our observations with multiple \[C II\]  datasets from the literature, both at low and high redshift"}]},"citation":"Stacey1991, Stacey2010, Gullberg2015, Capak2015, Diaz-Santos2017, Cormier2015, Brauher2008, Contursi2017, Magdis2014, Brisbin2015, Accurso2017, etc."},{"what":{"value":"Herschel/Spitzer deblended photometry for the targets","evidence":[{"loc":"2.4 Continuum emission","quote":"together with the available *Spitzer* and *Herschel* data (cite: Elbaz2011)"}]},"citation":"Elbaz2011"}],"simulations_or_models_as_data":[{"value":"Depletion-time vs sSFR models of Sargent2014 and Scoville2017 compared with [CII]/IR","evidence":[{"loc":"3.3","quote":"we considered two models ((cite: Sargent2014), (cite: Scoville2017)) predicting how the depletion time of galaxies changes as a function of their distance from the main-sequence"}]}],"calibration":[{"field":"pipeline_or_manual","value":"Standard ALMA pipeline (CASA)","evidence":[{"loc":"2.3 [C II] emission line measurements","quote":"The data were reduced with the standard ALMA pipeline based on the CASA software (cite: McMullin2007)."}]}],"imaging":[{"field":"continuum_subtraction","value":"450 um continuum maps made excluding line-dominated channels; [C II] fluxes corrected for 158 um continuum measured or predicted from SED (avg 10%)","evidence":[{"loc":"2.4 Continuum emission","quote":"For the 450 $\mu$m continuum maps instead we made sure to exclude the channels where the flux is dominated by the \[C II\]  emission line."}]}],"inherited":[{"what":{"value":"Iterative uv-plane line search and extraction procedure","evidence":[{"loc":"2.3","quote":"similar to what described in Daddi et al. (2015 and in preparation) and (cite: Coogan2017)."}]},"from_reference":"Daddi et al. 2015; (cite: Coogan2017)"},{"what":{"value":"Pixel-by-pixel SED fitting for stellar mass/SFR maps","evidence":[{"loc":"2.1","quote":"following the method described by (cite: Cibinel2015)"}]},"from_reference":"(cite: Cibinel2015)"},{"what":{"value":"Redshift refinement with LBG templates","evidence":[{"loc":"2.1","quote":"we applied to our VLT/FORS2 and Keck UV rest-frame spectra the same approach described in (cite: Gobat2017)"}]},"from_reference":"(cite: Gobat2017)"},{"what":{"value":"IR SED fitting with Draine2007 models plus MBB, Monte Carlo errors, gas-to-dust ratio","evidence":[{"loc":"2.4","quote":"Following the method presented in (cite: Magdis2012), we fitted the IR photometry with (cite: Draine2007) models"}]},"from_reference":"(cite: Magdis2012)"}],"unstated_but_needed":["Exact CASA/pipeline version","Line-free channels and continuum channel selection for Band 9","Weights/flagging and visibility handling in GILDAS uv_fit","Flux calibrators and flux scale uncertainty","Detailed IR SED fit settings (beta, priors) beyond beta=2","Full literature table (only online)","Exact selection of channels used for the optimal-channel averaging"],"analysis_steps":[{"order":1,"goal":"Derive optical sizes and stellar mass/SFR maps","method":{"value":"Pixel-by-pixel SED fitting of HST images; exponential fit to mass maps with GALFIT","evidence":[{"loc":"2.3.1","quote":"using the GALFIT algorithm (cite: Peng2010)"}]},"software":["GALFIT"],"key_parameters":[],"assumptions":[{"value":"Bruzual2003 constant-SFR templates, Calzetti2000 extinction, solar metallicity, Chabrier IMF","evidence":[{"loc":"2.1","quote":"We corrected the fluxes for dust extinction following the prescriptions by (cite: Calzetti2000)."}]}],"fitting":{"value":"not stated","evidence":[]},"validation":{"value":"Masses agree with Santini2014 within <30%","evidence":[{"loc":"2.1","quote":"they differ $<$ 30% with no systematic trends"}]}},{"order":2,"goal":"Detect [C II] and extract spectra in uv plane","method":{"value":"Iterative uv-plane fits (PSF, Gaussian, exponential) channel by channel at HST-based positions, averaging optimal channels, iterating to convergence","evidence":[{"loc":"2.3","quote":"We fitted, in the *uv* plane, a given source model (PSF, but also Gaussian and exponential profiles, tailored to the *HST* size of the galaxies) to all four sidebands and channel per channel"}]},"software":["GILDAS"],"key_parameters":[{"value":"secure detection >5 sigma; tentative S/N>2.3 with 719 km/s averaging","evidence":[{"loc":"2.3.1","quote":"they have emission line significance $> 5 \sigma$ in the optimal channel range"}]}],"assumptions":[{"value":"HST positions shifted by DEC=-0.2" to align with ALMA","evidence":[{"loc":"B. Astrometry","quote":"In our analysis we adopt the following coordinate shifts $\Delta RA = 0$”, $\Delta DEC = -0.2$”."}]}],"fitting":{"value":"not stated","evidence":[]},"validation":{"value":"Redshifts from weighted mean frequency vs Gaussian fit consistent; MAD vs optical z 200 km/s","evidence":[{"loc":"2.3.1","quote":"median absolute deviation (MAD) of 200 km s$^{-1}$ (MAD$_{\rm z}=0.002$)"}]}},{"order":3,"goal":"Measure total [C II] fluxes and sizes, stack","method":{"value":"uv_fit of exponential model with size/center fixed from optical; stacking of aligned visibilities; size free in stack","evidence":[{"loc":"2.3.1","quote":"We then extracted the \[C II\]  flux by fitting the ALMA data in the $uv$ plane, using the Fourier Transform of the 2D exponential model, with the GILDAS task `uv_fit`."}]},"software":["GILDAS","CASA"],"key_parameters":[],"assumptions":[{"value":"[C II] size follows optical size","evidence":[{"loc":"2.3.1","quote":"This indicates that on average the optical sizes that we used in the analysis are appropriate for the fit of our ALMA data"}]}],"fitting":{"value":"Least-squares uv fits; uncertainties from GILDAS","evidence":[]},"validation":{"value":"uvmodelfit and Gaussian model give consistent fluxes; simulations in Appendix A","evidence":[{"loc":"2.3.1","quote":"We checked that fluxes and uncertainties determined with the `uvmodelfit` task provided by CASA would give consistent results."}]}},{"order":4,"goal":"Continuum fluxes, IR SED fitting, dust and gas masses","method":{"value":"Exponential-profile uv fits of 450/850 um continuum; Draine2007 + MBB SED fits; Mmol from gas-to-dust ratio and from Schmidt-Kennicutt relation","evidence":[{"loc":"2.4","quote":"we fitted the IR photometry with (cite: Draine2007) models, supplemented by the use of a single temperature modified black body (MBB) fit"}]},"software":["GILDAS"],"key_parameters":[],"assumptions":[{"value":"Metallicity from Zahid2014 mass-metallicity relation; delta_GDR per Magdis2012; Sargent2014 integrated SK relation","evidence":[{"loc":"2.4","quote":"Given their stellar mass and the mass-metallicity relation by (cite: Zahid2014) we estimated their gas phase metallicity."}]}],"fitting":{"value":"Weighted by uncertainties; Monte Carlo errors","evidence":[{"loc":"2.4","quote":"Uncertainties on $L_{\mathrm{IR}}$ and $M_{\mathrm{dust}}$ were quantified using Monte Carlo simulations"}]},"validation":{"value":"Both gas mass methods consistent for 850um-detected galaxies","evidence":[{"loc":"2.4","quote":"we concluded that both methods give consistent results"}]}},{"order":5,"goal":"Fit L[CII]-Mmol relation and alpha_[CII] with literature","method":{"value":"Linear fit of log L[CII] vs log Mmol; median alpha_[CII] for subsamples; tests vs metallicity, sSFR, redshift","evidence":[{"loc":"3.2","quote":"$$\begin{equation}
\log L_{\mathrm{[C~{\small II}]}} = -1.28(\pm 0.21) + 0.98(\pm 0.02) \log M_{\mathrm{mol}}
\end{equation}$$"}]},"software":[],"key_parameters":[],"assumptions":[{"value":"alpha_CO: log alpha_CO = 0.64 - 1.5(12+log(O/H)-8.7); metallicities converted to Pettini2004 scale","evidence":[{"loc":"3.4","quote":"We converted the CO luminosity into gas mass by assuming the following $\alpha_{\mathrm{CO}}$ – metallicity dependence"}]}],"fitting":{"value":"not stated","evidence":[]},"validation":{"value":"Slopes of -1 or -2 for alpha_CO give same conclusions","evidence":[{"loc":"3.4","quote":"would not change our conclusions"}]}}],"software":[{"name":"CASA","version":"not stated","used_for":{"value":"Pipeline reduction, simobserve simulations, uvmodelfit checks","evidence":[{"loc":"2.3","quote":"The data were reduced with the standard ALMA pipeline based on the CASA software (cite: McMullin2007)."}]}},{"name":"GILDAS","version":"not stated","used_for":{"value":"uv-plane analysis (uv_fit) of line and continuum","evidence":[{"loc":"2.3","quote":"analyzed with the software GILDAS (cite: Guilloteau2000)"}]}},{"name":"GALFIT","version":"not stated","used_for":{"value":"Exponential fits to stellar mass maps","evidence":[{"loc":"2.3.1","quote":"using the GALFIT algorithm (cite: Peng2010)"}]}}],"results_numeric":[{"quantity":"Secure [C II] detections","value":"4 secure + 2 tentative of 10","uncertainty":"not stated","units":"galaxies","from_step":2,"evidence":[{"loc":"abstract","quote":"We detect \[C II\] from six galaxies (four secure, two tentative)"}]},{"quantity":"Stacked L[CII]/LIR (7 galaxies)","value":"1.94e-3","uncertainty":"+0.34/-0.32 e-3","units":"dimensionless","from_step":3,"evidence":[{"loc":"2.3.3","quote":"is $(1.94^{+0.34}_{-0.32})\times 10^{-3}$"}]},{"quantity":"[C II] exponential scale length (stack of 4 detections)","value":"0.65","uncertainty":"0.15","units":"arcsec","from_step":3,"evidence":[{"loc":"2.3.1","quote":"We get an exponential scale length for the \[C II\]  emission of $0.65\pm0.15''$"}]},{"quantity":"L[CII]-Mmol relation","value":"log L = -1.28 + 0.98 log Mmol","uncertainty":"±0.21 (intercept), ±0.02 (slope)","units":"dimensionless","from_step":5,"evidence":[{"loc":"3.2","quote":"$$\begin{equation}
\log L_{\mathrm{[C~{\small II}]}} = -1.28(\pm 0.21) + 0.98(\pm 0.02) \log M_{\mathrm{mol}}
\end{equation}$$"}]},{"quantity":"Median alpha_[CII] (all main-sequence)","value":"31","uncertainty":"MAD 0.2 dex","units":"Msun/Lsun","from_step":5,"evidence":[{"loc":"3.2","quote":"we get a median $\alpha_{\mathrm{[C~{\small II}]}} = 31$ M$_\odot$/L$_\odot$ with a median absolute deviation of 0.2 dex"}]},{"quantity":"Median alpha_[CII] SPT lensed sample","value":"22","uncertainty":"not stated","units":"Msun/Lsun","from_step":5,"evidence":[{"loc":"3.2","quote":"We obtained a median $\alpha_{\mathrm{[CII]}} = 22$ M$_\odot$/L$_\odot$ for this sample"}]},{"quantity":"alpha_[CII] vs metallicity slope","value":"-0.2","uncertainty":"0.2","units":"dimensionless","from_step":5,"evidence":[{"loc":"3.4","quote":"we obtain a slope of $-0.2 \pm 0.2$"}]}],"findings_qualitative":[{"value":"z~2 main-sequence galaxies are not [C II] deficient, ~10x higher L[CII]/LIR than starbursts","evidence":[{"loc":"abstract","quote":"similar to that of local main-sequence galaxies ($\sim2\times10^{-3}$), and $\sim$ 10 times higher than that of starbursts"}]}],"claims":[{"hypothesis":"z~2 main-sequence galaxies are [C II] deficient like local (U)LIRGs","experiment":"ALMA Band 9 [C II] of 10 galaxies, L[CII]/LIR compared with literature","result":"Ratio ~1.9e-3, similar to local MS","finding":"Not deficient; ratio set by star formation mode/depletion time","support":"supported","evidence":[{"loc":"3.1","quote":"Our sample shows a $L_{\mathrm{[C~{\small II}]}}/L_{\mathrm{IR}}$ ratio comparable to that observed for local main-sequence sources"}]},{"hypothesis":"L[CII] traces molecular gas mass","experiment":"Combined sample with literature gas masses","result":"Linear relation, dispersion 0.3 dex, alpha ~31","finding":"[CII] is a convenient molecular gas tracer independent of MS/SB, metallicity, redshift","support":"supported","evidence":[{"loc":"3.2","quote":"We find that indeed L$_{\mathrm{[C~{\small II}]}}$ and M$_{\mathrm{mol}}$ are linearly correlated"}]},{"hypothesis":"[C II] emission is as extended as the stellar disk","experiment":"uv-plane stack with free size","result":"0.65±0.15 arcsec scale length","finding":"[C II] extent consistent with optical size","support":"supported","evidence":[{"loc":"2.3.1","quote":"We get an exponential scale length for the \[C II\]  emission of $0.65\pm0.15''$"}]}],"reasoning":[{"field":"why_this_data","value":"Band 9 needed to target [C II] at z~1.7-1.9 for typical MS galaxies in GOODS-S","evidence":[{"loc":"2.1","quote":"having spectroscopic redshift in the range $1.73 < z < 1.94$ to target the \[C II\]  emission line in ALMA Band 9"}]}],"alternatives_considered_or_rejected":[{"value":"PSF model rejected for total flux as it would underestimate fluxes for extended sources","evidence":[{"loc":"2.3.1","quote":"whereas by using a PSF model instead we would have underestimated the fluxes"}]}],"limitations_admitted":[{"value":"Fluxes depend critically on assumed model size from optical images; sizes not constrained individually","evidence":[{"loc":"2.3.1","quote":"the returned fluxes critically depend on the model size that we used and that we determined from the optical images"}]},{"value":"Higher-resolution configuration than requested caused loss of effective depth","evidence":[{"loc":"2.2 Details of ALMA observations","quote":"we obtained a flux measurement error 5 – 10 times higher than expected"}]}],"referee_caveats_inferred":["Small sample with 4 secure detections; stacks include a non-detection (ID2910)","Gas masses for literature samples heterogeneous (CO with varying alpha_CO, SK relation), and correlation partly circular for SK-based masses","Exponential size assumed from optical for flux","Stack excludes undetected sources, possibly biasing the ratio high"],"reproducibility":[{"field":"data_public_as_stated","value":"Project listed in acknowledgements; spectroscopic redshifts publicly available","evidence":[{"loc":"Acknowledgments","quote":"This paper makes use of the following ALMA data: ADS/JAO.ALMA#2012.1.00775.S"}]}],"code_released":[],"missing_for_reproduction":["CASA version","Channel selections","Full literature compilation (online only)","Specific SED-fit configuration"],"estimated_data_volume_inferred":"~tens of GB (10 short Band 9 and Band 7 EBs with fine spectral channels)","score_inferred":3,"score_reason":"Public data and clear uv-fitting recipe, but key inputs (optical sizes, SED fits, literature compilation) and versions are partly unspecified.","rediscovery_candidate":false,"rediscovery_reason":"Main results depend on heavy ancillary data and literature compilation, with iterative bespoke GILDAS procedures.","methods_papers":[{"citation":"Coogan2017","why":"Simulations of similar line detection procedure"},{"citation":"Magdis2012","why":"IR SED fitting and gas-to-dust ratio"},{"citation":"Cibinel2015","why":"Resolved stellar mass and SFR maps"}],"companion_papers":[{"citation":"Daddi et al. 2015","why":"Source of uv-plane extraction procedure"}],"related_projects_or_surveys":["GOODS-S","CANDELS","GMASS","GOALS","xCOLD GASS"]}
